[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/verify.py:66-66 - Extremely large receipt file (e.g., deeply nested JSON) could cause MemoryError. MemoryError is intentionally not caught, causing an unhandled exception that may crash the caller.
[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/verify.py:215-215 - run_verify now returns VerifyResult with reason starting with 'corrupt receipt:'. Callers that parse the reason string expecting previous error messages (e.g., 'excerpt missing required fields') will break.
